we can't get enough of frozen it gave us  two of the most beloved Disney  Princesses of all time while Elsa may be  in the spotlight Anna is actually pretty  interesting now let's dive into the  secret history of Anna from frozen Anna  from frozen is one of the most beloved  Disney Princesses of all time  she and her sister Elsa are so popular  they became their own franchise her  sweet strong and optimistic personality  make her an awesome role model fans all  over the world can't get enough of this  Scandinavian sweetheart and neither can  we  we love Anna and wanted to take a closer  look at her fascinating secret history  there's a lot to her both behind and in  front of the camera before we sink our  teeth into the juicy secrets of this  character let's take a look at the  secret history that created her tens of  time and careful consideration was put  into the development of Anna let's see  just how deep Disney delve to bring this  joyful princess to life three voices  Anna is voiced by the incredibly  talented Kristen Bell she's won a Golden  Globe for Best Actress for her role on  the TV show at the good place with a  powerhouse like that behind the mic Anna  was sure to be a hit the creators of the  film loved Kristen so much that they  infused a ton of her features and  personality into her character animators  confirms that they took quite a lot of  inspiration for honest features and  expressions from Kristen they also  wanted to give her some of the actors  awkward but bubbly personality they even  included some of Kristen's quirks  Anna has an adorable catchphrase over  and over in the movie she asks her  signature question how many times have  you heard on a pause and ask wait what  did you know that Disney riders added  those words to the script because the  actor who voices Anna Kristen Bell  provides the voice for grownup Anna she  apparently has a habit of asking the  same question in real life the writing  team was so taken by Kristen and her  quirk that they decided to weave it into  the movie other characters get in on the  cute homage to Kristoff Olaf and even  Elsa get in on the action this adorable  line infuses more of the star's perky  personality into the film we love this  adorable phrase and we're so glad the  creators weaved it into the script  Kristen Val isn't the only voice to  massively influence what we hear when we  think of Anna did you know that one  point in the film  people provided the voice of this  red-haired princess during the epic song  do you want to build a snowman it took a  total of three talented actors to bring  on it to life Katie Lopez provides the  voice for the youngest version of Anna  in the song katie is a talents legacy  both of her parents are accomplished  actors her mom Kristen anderson-lopez  lent her voice to films like Coco and  Ralph breaks the Internet  her dad Robert Lopez is an award-winning  writer he helped create Avenue Q and the  Book of Mormon that's a pretty  impressive family of talented creators  Agatha Lehmann provides the voice of  adolescent Anna in the song she's also  got a lot of talents in her family her  mom has written for wreckit-ralph a  wrinkle in time and much more she's also  the director of frozen having a woman  direct an animated feature was a Disney  first Kristen Bell provides the voice  for teenaged Anna and continues to voice  her for the rest of the film she helps  us transition to the very grown-up  princess who unites her kingdom and  saves her sister from exile it's no  surprise it took so much talent to voice  this dynamic character the choices in  voice acting blend perfectly to create  the illusion of watching Anna grow up  the film frozen is based on a classic  tale called The Snow Queen the book was  written by Dutch author Hans Christian  Andersen the creators of the film  decided to honor the author of the  original story with their own character  creations some of the characters names  are a playful nod to the beloved writer  Hans Kristoff Anna and Sven all have the  privilege of being part of this sweet  nod their names together sound a little  bit like the authors when you say them  quickly we can't help but find that  detail adorable it did awesome way to  honor the man who laid the groundwork  for the story to develop frozen isn't  the only Disney story he created he also  wrote The Little Mermaid his stories  lend themselves perfectly to the Disney  formula of storytelling his versions are  a bit more grown-up but the building  blocks are there the relationship  between Elsa and Anna is a foundation of  the entire story the bonds between these  sisters is what makes the entire movie  work understanding that special bond  between sisters was essential for the  filmmakers the creators held a sister  summit in order to better understand a  sisterhood and  help create onna our perfect princess  didn't just happen by accident  the production team called together  women from all over the studio who had  grown up with sisters they spent hours  discussing their experiences and what  sisterhood meant to them I like the open  gates we are never closing them again  the creator's took all of this  information and wove it into one of the  best character relationships in Disney  history if all of this behind the scenes  info wasn't enough reason for you to  fall head over heels in love with onna  this next fact is sure to win you over  onna literally saved the film without  her there wouldn't even be a frozen for  us to freak out about when Disney  creators first tried to adapt the Ice  Queen to an animated feature they  struggled the main character was just  too problematic for them to turn into a  family-friendly princess at first Elsa  was an icy villain with nothing to make  the audience love her it seemed like a  concept that was doomed  but the creator's refused to let it go  there were several versions of the story  written and scrapped before they hit on  the secret sauce that makes the movie  work once they introduced the character  of Anna everything fell into place the  dynamic relationship between the sisters  made the story much more relatable and  softens the character of Elsa  it wasn't until Anna's upbeat  personality was added to the mix that  frozen was born and the rest is Disney  history from the moment frozen was  conceived anna has played a huge part in  making the film a hit so much went into  making the optimistic princess we've  talked about all the secrets behind her  creation and developments but what about  Anna as a character  trust us she has plenty of hidden  history too let's start with a Disney  theory that spans four films and nearly  two decades of Disney history it's been  discussed all over the Internet's by  fans around the globe when the gates of  arendelle are open for Elsa's coronation  guests arrive from all over the world  this is a huge event for the royal  family dignitaries from other kingdoms  come to pay their respects to the late  king and queen but also to witness the  crowning of a new leader while Lana  sings for the first time in forever she  greets the incoming crowd in one frame  we see a famous couple who provide a  hint at a family secret Eugene and  Rapunzel can be seen entering the city  to attend the coronation cameos like  this are never simple or meaningless in  the Disney Universe  there is a reason rip on  shows up mm-hmm big summer blowout  Rapunzel and Ana are actually cousins  their families ruled two separates and  distant kingdoms but they're related  Rapunzel had been held captive for so  long that she never got to know her  cousins in arendelle as soon as she  heard about the passing of her aunt and  uncle she must have been devastated she  had to make an appearance at the  coronation to meet her long-lost family  and get to know her cousins Disney has  confirmed that when the king and queen  passed away at sea they had been on  their way to a wedding this fits the  exact timeline of when Rapunzel and  Eugene were tying the knot knowing that  her aunt and uncle lost their lives on  the way to her wedding must have been  tough for Princess Rapunzel a secret  cousin is pretty juicy stuff it's not  every day you find out you have a  relative you never knew about  Rapunzel isn't the only missing piece to  Ana's family history after her parents  left arendelle a whole new chapter in  the secret family history would be added  the death of the king and queen is a  major catalyst for the movie if they had  returned home the story would have met  it's happily ever after about ten  minutes in what if the king and queen  didn't die during the shipwreck this may  be the biggest secret in Ana's history  her parents ship was destroyed and they  were never heard from again  that much is true and they would  eventually die they actually survived  the shipwreck and found their way to a  jungle island they built themselves a  shelter and found ways to feed  themselves while on the islands the  Queen fell pregnant she and her husband  welcomed their handsome baby boy into  the world separated from their loving  daughters shortly after their bouncing  baby boy was born the king and queen  finally met their end they were killed  by the big cats that they shared their  jungle home with their son was spared  and was soon as opted his gorilla family  named him Tarzan they made sure the baby  was kept safe and thrived  Ana's secret little brother lives the  tie between frozen tangled and Tarzan is  epic secret family ties long-lost little  brothers and cousins reunited are about  as exciting as it gets this one event  ties in one more of the Disney Universe  in the Little Mermaid Ariel stores her  human artifacts in a sunken shipwreck  observant fans have noticed that the  king and queen of arendelle set sail in  a ship that looks exactly like the one  Ariel spends her time in that means that  at least for Disney film  are all tied together by honest parents  and their faithful trip may be the best  part of this four-way tie in is that  it's largely been confirmed directly by  Disney creators  during a reddit AMA fans asked where the  king and queen were headed on their  fateful trip writer and director  Jennifer Lee confirmed they were headed  to a wedding at the exact same time that  Rapunzel and Eugene were about to be  married co-director Chris buck further  clarifies that the king and queen didn't  die in a shipwreck  he told fans of the king and queen  survived lost at sea for weeks before  they landed on a lush jungle island  there they built themselves a home next  to a family of gorillas it's worth  noting that Chris has the inside scoop  on another Disney film he was also the  director of Tarzan if anyone was  qualified to confirm the link between  the two films it's him the rich  character development of frozen helped  make it the international sensation it  is today Disney creators knocked it out  of the park when they created Anna her  addition to the story made the entire  film possible without the masterfully  written relationship between her and  Elsa the story would be lacking its  heart Anna breathes the soul into frozen  it's her optimism and sheer  determination that brings her sister  back from the brink her hidden history  is a rich part of the story that we  think everyone should know we hope you  loved looking behind the curtain at what  makes honest such a dynamic character  what's your favorite thing about Anna is  there something about her you just can't  resist let us know in the comments below  what you love about this perky princess  we love sharing these disney secrets  with you and we hope you love learning  them we'll see you next time  [Music]  [Music]
 

